; worldroad.eval — the road hurts, and camp is how you answer it (P3.5).
;
; Michael, 2026-09-09: "DoT should still affect the party members. Travelling on
; the world map COULD easily kill affected members." Before P3.5 a journey
; settled SUPPLIES only, so a poisoned party travelled for free.
;
; THE DOSE IS THE HARD PART, and both extremes measure nothing:
;   - a small DoT is out-healed. Health regen runs while walking (nothing about
;     travel sets the exertion gate), and at ~0.23/s it beats any poison that
;     does not also kill outright. So "arrives with less health" is not a
;     measurable claim over an hour of road.
;   - a huge one kills inside the FIRST slice, which proves the tick happens and
;     nothing else — and then `camp` reports "recovered" over four corpses,
;     because rest excludes the dead by design.
; So this measures the thing that is unambiguous: a party ALREADY on the floor
; is finished by its DoT ON THE ROAD, where before it would have arrived intact.
logecho on
reset
encounters off
leave

; --- wounded to the floor, then poisoned, then made to walk ------------------
; bleed downs them; poison is what finishes a downed member (the overkill rule).
effect bleed 0 6 4
effect bleed 1 6 4
effect bleed 2 6 4
effect bleed 3 6 4
effect poison 0 0.5 600
party
travel e 1
party

; --- a healthy party camps: hours pass, supplies pay, health returns ---------
reset
leave
effect bleed 0 6 4
travel e 1
party
supplies
camp
party
supplies
world
